          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\n**History of Present Illness:**  \nThe patient has focal epilepsy with focal impaired-awareness seizures, beginning at age 37. The epilepsy has a genetic etiology due to a causative **SCN1A c.5734C>T** variant. Seizures are drug-responsive.\n\n**Current Antiseizure Medications:**  \n- Zonisamide  \n- Perampanel  \n\n**Seizure Burden:**  \nApproximately one focal impaired-awareness seizure per year.\n\n**Assessment:**  \nDrug-responsive focal epilepsy with focal impaired-awareness seizures, associated with the causative SCN1A c.5734C>T variant.\n\n**Plan:**  \nContinue zonisamide and perampanel. Continue monitoring seizure frequency.\n\nSincerely,  \nEpilepsy Clinic",
